  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Learn to Read</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Laos):  Learn to Read is a five-year activity that improves classroom instruction by providing teaching and learning materials; enhancing teacher competencies through training and classroom support; and strengthening community engagement in helping children learn to read. These activities aim to  improve the quality of basic education in Laos, with a special focus on children who do not speak Lao at home, and children with disabilities. This activity supports the development of literacy for children from pre-primary to second grade by strengthening the literacy environment in school and at home through targeted engagement of community members. In addition to teacher training, interventions include face-to-face home visits by literacy volunteers and Village Education Development Committees, reading festivals, and family literacy days at schools. USAID and its implementing partners Save the Children, Room to Read, and Humanity &amp; Inclusion, work with the Ministry of Education and Sports, the Ministry of Information, Culture and Tourism, and other development partners to determine effective strategies that enhance commitment to literacy and strengthen the school, home and community literacy environment.A stronger basic education system will advance Laos&apos; national development objectives and USG goals in the basic education sector. In the long term, improved education outcomes will create more opportunities for Lao children and youth as they move toward adulthood, giving Laos&apos; overwhelmingly young population the tools they need to help their country achieve greater economic independence.  Learn to Read will also help Laos recover from the negative impacts of COVID-19 on the educational system: school closures, budget cuts, and challenges related to adapting to online learning methods.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives for Laos: The USAID Learn to Read activity aims to: 1) Improves the Lao reading ability of students in pre-primary and early primary education; 2) Improves classroom instruction; 3) Enhances teacher competencies in applying effective classroom teaching and learning activities and their access to resources to meet the needs of targeted children; 4) Strengthens community engagement and the development of conducive learning environments for improved reading skills, particularly for children who do not speak Lao and children with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
